  },
  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup almond flour",
    "2 tablespoon psyllium husk powder",
    "2 tablespoon parmesan cheese",
    "1 teaspoon italian seasoning",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "6 ounce mozzarella cheese (grated)",
    "2 tablespoon cream cheese (softened)",
    "1 large egg",
    "1 medium fresh tomatoes",
    "4 ounce cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1/4 cup low-carb tomato sauce (such as Rao's)",
    "2/3 medium red bell pepper (or any other color)",
    "2 tablespoon fresh basil"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Start by measuring the dry ingredients and spices into a bowl. Add in the almond flour, psyllium husk, parmesan, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7486.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl, measure out the mozzarella cheese.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7492.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Microwave the cheese for 40–50 seconds until completely melted and pliable. Add the cream cheese on top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7494.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the egg to the dry ingredients and mix them together a little bit.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7495.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the melted mozzarella cheese and cream cheese to the dry ingredient mixture and mix everything together. Don't be afraid to get your hands dirty — they're the best tool for the job here. You might get a bit messy, but it'll be oh so worth it in the end!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7498.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Separate the dough into equal portions. Roll the dough balls out quite thin — you want them to be about 1/4\" thick. You can use the top of a pot or other large round object to cut out your pizza base. You can form the circles by hand, but mine always seem to turn out oval. When I work with this dough, I like to use a Silpat because they're naturally nonstick and make things a lot easier.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7504.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fold the edges of the dough inward to form a small crust on the dough. If you have any scraps remaining, you can add these to the crust if you'd like.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7507.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 10 minutes — just long enough so that they're starting to turn a light golden brown.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7510.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove crusts from the oven and let cool for a moment.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7517.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the tomato and add it to the pizzas along with the tomato sauce. (Aww, they look like little peace signs!).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7520.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Top the pizzas with shredded cheddar.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7524.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice up the bell peppers. You can use whatever colors you'd like — I'm using red and yellow.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7528.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arrange the peppers on top and throw the pizzas back in the oven for another 8–10 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7534.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven and let cool. In the meantime, slice up some fresh basil into thin strips.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_7540.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Top with basil, serve, and enjoy the fresh bites of summer!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/fresh-bell-pepper-basil-pizza/#wprm-recipe-51225-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/PizzaLong1.jpg"
    }
  ],
